Enfold
======

A local-first SQLite memory service with provenance, current-state rules,
and a Unix-socket daemon. There is no hosted service. Distribution is
GitHub-only under the MIT License.

This project builds on prior work, gratefully credited:

- The holographic memory provider (the `MemoryProvider` integration, HRR
  retrieval, the SQLite fact store, trust scoring, and entity resolution)
  was created by **dusterbloom** for NousResearch/hermes-agent (PR #2351)
  and is licensed MIT. Parts of that foundation remain in this tree.

- Holographic Reduced Representations, the vector-symbolic technique
  underlying holographic retrieval, are due to **Tony A. Plate**,
  "Holographic Reduced Representations," IEEE Transactions on Neural
  Networks, 6(3):623-641, 1995.

Enfold is a standalone daemon and MCP bridge. It is not a Hermes plugin.
The optional Hermes staging adapter lives in
`integrations/hermes_enfold_v1` and is not installed by Enfold.

